Implements the requested app: photograph a gym machine → get step-by-step instructions on how to use it. Built as a client-side React + TypeScript + Vite SPA, no backend required.

## Architecture

- **`src/types/machine.ts`** — `GymMachine` type with steps, muscles, tips, warnings, difficulty, keywords
- **`src/data/machines.ts`** — Static database of 16 machines across 8 categories (Chest, Back, Legs, Shoulders, Arms, Core, Cardio, Full Body)
- **`src/hooks/useMachineIdentifier.ts`** — Identification logic: scores machines by keyword overlap with filename; falls back to a shuffled shortlist when no match found
- **`src/components/ImageUploader.tsx`** — File picker + drag-and-drop + `getUserMedia` camera capture
- **`src/components/MachineCard.tsx`** — Browse grid tile
- **`src/components/MachineGuide.tsx`** — Full guide: numbered steps, primary/secondary muscles, pro tips, safety warnings
- **`src/App.tsx`** — Three-view SPA: `home` (identify) → `results` → `guide`; `browse` → `guide`

## Views

| Home / Identify | Browse Machines | Machine Guide |
|---|---|---|
| ![Home](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/81e3a734-9e18-4b3b-9331-63f015c37aff) | ![Browse](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/46ab744f-f2b2-4cbc-a5d2-a6b1fea7e363) | ![Guide](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/baeb6a8d-c7de-434a-8bec-6f772241f543) |

## Identification flow

```ts
// Scores each machine by keyword overlap with the uploaded filename.
// Falls back to a random shortlist so the user can manually pick.
const scored = GYM_MACHINES.map((machine) => {
  let score = 0;
  for (const kw of machine.keywords) {
    if (filename.includes(kw.toLowerCase())) score += kw.length;
  }
  return { machine, score };
});
```

Confidence-ranked results are presented for the user to confirm — avoids silent misidentification.

