<summary>Original prompt</summary>

## Problem

Building the app fails with:

```
mercantis core/mercantis_coreApp.swift:13:30 Type 'UIShellRouter' does not conform to protocol 'ObservableObject'
```

The error originates from this line in `mercantis core/mercantis_coreApp.swift`:

```swift
@StateObject private var shellRouter = UIShellRouter()
```

## Root cause

`UIShellRouter` is declared in `mercantis core/UIShell/NavigationShell.swift` as:

```swift
@MainActor
final class UIShellRouter: ObservableObject {
    @Published var selectedSection: NavigationSection? = .home
    @Published var setupDestination: SetupDestination = .overview
    ...
}
```

Under Swift 6 / strict concurrency, the class is `@MainActor` isolated, but the `ObservableObject` protocol's `objectWillChange` requirement is non-isolated. An actor-isolated type cannot satisfy a non-isolated protocol requirement, so the conformance is rejected with the misleading "does not conform to protocol 'ObservableObject'" message. The error surfaces at the `@StateObject` use site in `mercantis_coreApp.swift` because that is where the conformance is first required.

## Fix

Remove the class-level `@MainActor` attribute from `UIShellRouter` in `mercantis core/UIShell/NavigationShell.swift`. The router is only ever used from `@StateObject`, SwiftUI `App`, and `View.body` contexts, all of which are already MainActor-isolated, so removing the class-level annotation does not change runtime behavior but allows the `ObservableObject` conformance to compile cleanly.

Change:

```swift
@MainActor
final class UIShellRouter: ObservableObject {
```

to:

```swift
final class UIShellRouter: ObservableObject {
```

Do not change anything else in the file. Do not modify any other files. Verify the project still builds.

